  C1: scljet-update-ipk-column-silently-ignored + scljet-update-ipk-does-not-move-rowid — one
      defect, two entries. An INTEGER PRIMARY KEY column IS the rowid, so UPDATE t SET <ipk>=N
      must RE-KEY the row (delete + reinsert at the new rowid, duplicate => error like
      leafInsertCell), and index entries store the rowid as their tail so they must move too.
      Today executeUpdate rewrites the record field at the existing rowid and reports Right.
  C2: scljet-insert-null-literal-rejected — INSERT ... VALUES (..., NULL, ...) fails in any
      position with "expected a literal in WHERE" while UPDATE ... SET x = NULL parses fine.
      INSERT's value-list literal reader is the suspect (and its error text misnames the clause).
  Ground truth is real sqlite3, not our own output: both bugs are recorded with measured
  reference behaviour. Write the failing repro FIRST, in the real harness, before fixing.
next: locate the engine write path (executeUpdate / parseValueList) and reproduce C1 + C2 against
  real sqlite3 before touching code.
